  <task-lists disabled sortable>
    <div class="comment-body markdown-body js-comment-body soft-wrap user-select-contain d-block">
      <p dir="auto">Addresses <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="4572852965" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/25875" data-hovercard-type="issue" data-hovercard-url="/openai/codex/issues/25875/hovercard" href="https://github.com/openai/codex/issues/25875">#25875</a>.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Summary</h2>
<p dir="auto"><code class="notranslate">hooks.json</code> accepted unknown top-level fields. A file with <code class="notranslate">SessionStart</code> at the root parsed as an empty hook configuration without warning.</p>
<h2 dir="auto">Repro</h2>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="{ &quot;SessionStart&quot;: [...] }"><pre class="notranslate">{ <span class="pl-ent">"SessionStart"</span>: [<span class="pl-ii">...</span>] }</pre></div>
<p dir="auto">Previously: zero hooks, zero warnings.</p>
<p dir="auto">Now:</p>
<div class="snippet-clipboard-content notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="unknown field `SessionStart`, expected `hooks`"><pre lang="text" class="notranslate"><code class="notranslate">unknown field `SessionStart`, expected `hooks`
</code></pre></div>
<p dir="auto">The supported shape remains:</p>
<div class="highlight highlight-source-json notranslate position-relative overflow-auto" dir="auto" data-snippet-clipboard-copy-content="{ &quot;hooks&quot;: { &quot;SessionStart&quot;: [...] } }"><pre class="notranslate">{ <span class="pl-ent">"hooks"</span>: { <span class="pl-ent">"SessionStart"</span>: [<span class="pl-ii">...</span>] } }</pre></div>
<h2 dir="auto">Fix</h2>
<p dir="auto">Reject unknown top-level fields and surface the parse warning in human and JSONL <code class="notranslate">codex exec</code> output.</p>
    </div>
  </task-lists>
  
</div>

